ing can improve while hospitals absorb coverage loss</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Oscar=E2=80=99s third-quarter revenue =
increased to $5.14 billion from $2.99 billion, its MLR declined to 84.0% from=
 88.5%, and operating income improved to $178 million from a $129 million los=
s. Membership reached 2.69 million, and updated risk-adjustment estimates con=
tributed $250 million to revenue. Oscar raised full-year operating-income gui=
dance to $850 million-$950 million from $600 million-$800 million. (<a href=
=3D"https://ir.oscarhealth.com/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001568651=
-26-000082/oscarhealththirdquarter202.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decora=
tion:underline;">Oscar Health, <em>Third Quarter 2026 Results</em>, November =
5, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The result does not refute last week=
=E2=80=99s finding that Exchange attrition is increasing hospital uncompensat=
ed care. It localizes the economics: disciplined rate increases and favorable=
 risk adjustment can improve carrier profitability on retained enrollment whi=
le providers bear losses when other consumers exit coverage.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The split raises the value of enrollme=
nt retention, premium-payment monitoring and eligibility intervention for bot=
h sides. Plans need accurate risk-adjustment and lapse management; hospitals =
need earlier identification of coverage loss before services convert to self-=
pay. Oscar=E2=80=99s $250 million adjustment also shows that risk-score perfo=
rmance remains a major earnings variable despite improved underlying underwri=
ting.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Final 2027 enrollment, payment-effectu=
ation rates and whether Oscar=E2=80=99s risk-adjustment advantage persists af=
ter market-wide data reconcile.</p>
